---
const prompt = `Inspect this Worker project and configure Cloudflare Workers Previews safely.

1. Read the Wrangler configuration file and identify vars, secrets, bindings, Durable Objects, Workflows, service bindings, queues, routes, cron triggers, observability, limits, placement, and any env sections.
2. Add or update a \`previews\` block for every binding or runtime setting that the Preview needs. Do not assume production bindings are available in Previews.
3. Do not point Previews at production KV, D1, R2, Hyperdrive, Vectorize, Queue, Workflow, or external resources unless I explicitly ask for that.
4. If the Worker uses same-Worker Durable Objects, keep the class in the same Worker so Previews get isolated DO state. If the code reads a Durable Object binding from \`env\`, declare that binding in \`previews\`.
5. Warn me if service bindings, Workflows, queue consumers, cron triggers, or routes need staging resources or alternate test paths with current Preview behavior.
6. If I use GitHub Actions, add a minimal workflow that runs \`wrangler preview --json\`, posts the Preview URL to the PR, and deletes the Preview when the PR closes. Prefer \`cloudflare/wrangler-action\` when it is enough.
7. Show the \`gh secret set\` commands needed for \`CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN\` and \`CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID\`.
8. After editing, summarize which production resources are isolated, which are shared, and which current Preview behaviors still affect this app.`;
---

<aside
	class="border-primary/70 bg-primary/5 not-prose my-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border"
	aria-label="Agent setup prompt"
>
	<div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 p-5 sm:p-6">
		<div class="min-w-0">
			<p
				class="text-muted-foreground mb-3 text-xs font-semibold tracking-[0.18em] uppercase"
			>
				For coding agents
			</p>
			<p
				class="text-foreground m-0 font-mono text-lg leading-relaxed sm:text-xl"
			>
				Configure Worker Previews for this project safely...
			</p>
			<p class="text-muted-foreground mt-3 mb-0 text-sm leading-relaxed">
				Copy this prompt into your coding agent to configure Previews from an
				existing Worker project.
			</p>
		</div>

		<button
			class="border-border bg-background hover:bg-muted focus-visible:outline-primary inline-flex shrink-0 cursor-copy items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border px-3 py-2 text-sm font-medium transition-colors focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2"
			type="button"
			data-worker-previews-agent-prompt
		>
			<svg
				aria-hidden="true"
				class="h-4 w-4"
				viewBox="0 0 24 24"
				fill="none"
				stroke="currentColor"
				stroke-width="2"
				stroke-linecap="round"
				stroke-linejoin="round"
			>
				<rect width="14" height="14" x="8" y="8" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
				<path d="M4 16c-1.1 0-2-.9-2-2V4c0-1.1.9-2 2-2h10c1.1 0 2 .9 2 2"
				></path>
			</svg>
			<span data-copy-label>Copy</span>
		</button>
	</div>

	<template data-worker-previews-agent-prompt-text>{prompt}</template>
</aside>

<script>
	function bindWorkerPreviewsAgentPrompt() {
		document
			.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(
				"[data-worker-previews-agent-prompt]",
			)
			.forEach((button) => {
				if (button.dataset.bound === "true") return;
				button.dataset.bound = "true";

				button.addEventListener("click", async () => {
					const prompt = button
						.closest("aside")
						?.querySelector<HTMLTemplateElement>(
							"[data-worker-previews-agent-prompt-text]",
						)?.content.textContent;
					if (!prompt) return;

					await navigator.clipboard.writeText(prompt.trim());
					const label = button.querySelector("[data-copy-label]");
					if (!label) return;

					const previousLabel = label.textContent;
					label.textContent = "Copied";
					setTimeout(() => {
						label.textContent = previousLabel;
					}, 1500);
				});
			});
	}

	bindWorkerPreviewsAgentPrompt();
	document.addEventListener("astro:page-load", bindWorkerPreviewsAgentPrompt);
</script>
